#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# subscript

#% text
# `subscript(x, i)` is the indexed name `x` with index `i` (several indices: `subscript(x, i, j)`). It has no definitions: it stays as written and can stand for a variable in algebra, calculus and equations. Notebooks show it with the indices below the name.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
subscript(a, 1 + 2)
#% output
#= subscript(a, 3)

#% cell
array((i, j) => subscript(a, i, j), [2, 2])
#% output
#= [[subscript(a, 1, 1), subscript(a, 1, 2)], [subscript(a, 2, 1), subscript(a, 2, 2)]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# As variables:

#% cell
solve(subscript(x, 1) + 2*subscript(x, 2) == 4, subscript(x, 1))
#% output
#= [[subscript(x, 1) -> 2*(2 - subscript(x, 2))]]

#% cell
d(subscript(x, 1)^3, subscript(x, 1))
#% output
#= 3*subscript(x, 1)^2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `array`, `table`
